## Risk Notes

1. PyQt6 and PyQt6-WebEngine are the decisive licensing factors. A permissive
   project license should not be used for public distribution unless commercial
   PyQt licensing is documented.
2. FFmpeg is currently fetched from a GPL build URL in `core.py`; avoid bundling
   that binary without notices and source-offer handling.
<<<<<<< HEAD
3. Bundled fonts are open-font assets, but their license files must stay with the
   redistributed package.
4. Re-run this audit whenever `requirements.txt`, `web_tools/package.json`,
   `fonts/open/open_fonts_manifest.json`, or the FFmpeg distribution strategy
   changes.
